  "id": "DrugBank_DB01122 - MONDO_18324",
  "verbalization": "Ambenonium is implicated in the pathogenesis of Adult-onset Myasthenia Gravis (AOMG) through a mechanism involving neuromuscular junction disease. The evidence suggests that Ambenonium is associated with Neuromuscular Junction Disease, which in turn is linked to both Neostigmine and Pyridostigmine, both of which are known to be used in the treatment of AOMG. This indicates a potential role of Ambenonium in the development or progression of AOMG, possibly through indirect effects on neuromuscular transmission. The high scores in the visible paths suggest a strong, albeit indirect, relationship between Ambenonium and AOMG, likely mediated by its interaction with neuromuscular junctions and the pharmacological properties of its analogs. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of neuromuscular junction dysfunction in AOMG, with Ambenonium potentially contributing to this dysfunction through its pharmacological profile.",
